{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 159533, "name": "Lincoln T", "username": "uberlinc", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/u/afea85/{size}.png", "created_at": "2022-10-20T11:22:11.167Z", "cooked": "<p>So, I’ve recently jumped to Fedora after considerable time on Ubuntu/Debian.<br>\nI’m trying to learn the ropes.</p>\n<p>I’ve had reasonable success with dnf and some .rpm files.<br>\nI’m trying to install vice Commodore Emulator and have a .rpm file.<br>\nWhen doing an rpm -i of the file, I get a long list of dependencies.</p>\n<p>I then go to look for those dependencies and see that they too have dependencies.</p>\n<p>Is there a quicker way than manually searching and installing a seemingly neverending tree of dependencies? (This could turn into a several hour/day job to install one single application!)</p>\n<p>Is there a magical way to have it search a repository and install all that is required?</p>\n<p>Thanks.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T19:27:15.347Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 149, "reads": 15, "readers_count": 14, "score": 798.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 54512, "topic_slug": "basic-question-re-installing-dependences", "display_username": "Lincoln T", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4241, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/basic-question-re-installing-dependences/54512/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 159124, "name": "FranciscoD", "username": "ankursinha", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/{size}/71_2.png", "created_at": "2022-10-20T12:09:56.368Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/uberlinc\">@uberlinc</a> , welcome to the community <img src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/2X/0/0af483d479044dd09776ea4487a85a311e4db052.png?v=12\" title=\":fedora:\" class=\"emoji emoji-custom\" alt=\":fedora:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"><br>\nPlease do take a look at the introductory posts in the <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#start-here</span> category if you’ve not had a chance to do so yet.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"uberlinc\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"54512\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/u/afea85/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Lincoln T:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When doing an rpm -i of the file, I get a long list of dependencies.</p>\n<p>I then go to look for those dependencies and see that they too have dependencies.</p>\n<p>Is there a quicker way than manually searching and installing a seemingly neverending tree of dependencies? (This could turn into a several hour/day job to install one single application!)</p>\n<p>Is there a magical way to have it search a repository and install all that is required?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes: use <code>dnf</code> <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">dnf install &lt;path to rpm file&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<p>will install the rpm, and resolve all dependencies from the repositories. This is the primary difference between rpm and <code>dnf</code>. <code>rpm</code> does not know about repositories, but <code>dnf</code> does. So <code>dnf</code> can pull in whatever dependencies are necessary from them (as long as they are present there).</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 3, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T22:39:24.005Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 13, "readers_count": 12, "score": 12.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 54512, "topic_slug": "basic-question-re-installing-dependences", "display_username": "FranciscoD", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 78, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [{"id": 4241, "username": "uberlinc", "name": "Lincoln T", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/u/afea85/{size}.png"}], "post_url": "/t/basic-question-re-installing-dependences/54512/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 158720, "name": "Lincoln T", "username": "uberlinc", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.c